# Copy to `.env.local` for local dev, and set the same variables in your host's
# dashboard (Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables).
#
# `neon deploy` writes the Neon values into .env.local for you — you shouldn't
# normally need to fill them in by hand.
#
# ONLY these reach the browser. Anything prefixed VITE_ is compiled into the
# public bundle, so NEVER put the Anthropic key, the YNAB token, or the
# Telegram token here — those stay server-side, in the function host's secrets
# (see CLAUDE.md).

# Neon project base URL, e.g. https://ep-example-123456.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/neondb
# The client derives both the auth and Data API endpoints from this. There is
# no publishable key to set: the session JWT is managed by the client, and
# row-level security is what actually protects the data.
VITE_NEON_DATABASE_URL=

# Where the assistant / daily-brief / schedule-setup functions are served from.
# No trailing slash. Whichever host they end up on, only this line changes.
VITE_FUNCTIONS_URL=
